    "background_story": "In the 14th century, Elowyn, a shrewd and cunning merchant, rose to prominence in the bustling trade hubs of medieval Europe. As a master of commerce, she navigated the complex web of tariffs and taxes with ease. However, when the kingdom imposed a hefty surtax on imported goods, Elowyn saw an opportunity to adapt and thrive. She cleverly diversified her trade routes, exploiting loopholes and forging alliances with neighboring merchants. Her business acumen and strategic thinking allowed her to not only weather the surtax storm but also expand her operations, amassing a vast fortune. Elowyn's success earned her a reputation as one of the most astute businesswomen of her time, and her legacy continued to inspire generations of entrepreneurs.",
